const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文用逐笔层面的价格形成框架，询问信息冲击和微观结构摩擦如何共同影响日内价格变化。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"The paper uses a transaction-level price-formation framework to ask how information shocks and microstructure frictions jointly affect intraday price changes. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/10.4.1035",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"来源构建并检验结构模型，分析日内买卖价差、波动、交易成本以及成交和报价自相关的模式。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It specifies and tests a structural model for intraday spreads, volatility, trading costs, and serial patterns in trades and quotes. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/10.4.1035",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要逐笔成交、同步报价、交易方向、交易成本定义、日内分段和交易场所制度资料。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"Required inputs are trades, synchronized quotes, trade direction, cost definitions, intraday partitions, and venue rules. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/10.4.1035",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"摘要描述其用于理解价格发现与有效交易成本的度量；这些度量依赖交易与报价数据，而不是只依赖收盘价。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The abstract presents measures for price discovery and effective trading cost that depend on trade-and-quote data rather than closing prices alone. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not convert association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/10.4.1035",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"统一成交与报价时钟，明确有效价差和报价价差的定义，处理撤单、更正及开收盘竞价，并保存市场状态标签。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Align trade and quote clocks; define effective and quoted spreads; handle cancellations, corrections, and auctions; retain market-state labels. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/10.4.1035",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Review of Financial Studies (1997)。该结构模型和原始 NYSE 制度不能被分钟蜡烛图复现，也不能自动给出另一场所的价格发现结论。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Review of Financial Studies (1997). The structural model and its NYSE institution cannot be reproduced from minute candles or automatically determine price discovery at another venue. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/10.4.1035",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Why Do Security Prices Change? A Transaction-Level Analysis of NYSE Stocks”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。该结构模型和原始 NYSE 制度不能被分钟蜡烛图复现，也不能自动给出另一场所的价格发现结论。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Why Do Security Prices Change? A Transaction-Level Analysis of NYSE Stocks”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
